格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"ADHD-friendly output shaping for DeepSeek Harness: one system-prompt section with adhd_on/adhd_off/adhd_status tools, persisted across restarts. Inspired by ayghri/i-have-adhd (MIT).","id":"gh:1347245974","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-i-have-adhd","slug":"yongshuai0314/dsh-i-have-adhd","topics":["accessibility","adhd","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","output-style"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"ADHD-friendly output shaping for DeepSeek Harness: one system-prompt section with adhd_on/adhd_off/a"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"dhd_status tools, persisted across restarts. Inspired by ayghri/i-have-adhd (MIT)."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-i-have-adhd"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"ADHD-friendly output shaping for DeepSeek Harness (DSH): one system-prompt section that rewrites how"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" the assistant replies — action first, numbered steps, concrete time estimates, zero preamble or clo"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"sers — with live on/off switches that persist across restarts."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"中文说明"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Inspired by ayghri/i-have-adhd (MIT). The ruleset here is an original rewrite for DSH; see THIRD-PAR"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ghri/i-have-adhd (MIT). The ruleset here is an original rewrite for DSH; see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What changes"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"| Before | After |"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| \"Great question! Let me think about this. Your auth flow has a few moving pieces: the middleware, "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"the token verification, and... Hope this helps!\" | \"Run `npm install jsonwebtoken@latest`, then edit"},{"id":"p8s3","text":" `src/auth.ts:42`. 1. Open the file 2. Replace `verifyToken` 3. Run the tests. Next: paste the first"},{"id":"p8s4","text":". 1. Open the file 2. Replace `verifyToken` 3. Run the tests. Next: paste the first failing line.\" |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- One system-prompt section (`dsh-i-have-adhd`, order 50 — after the persona, before tool guidance) "},{"id":"p10s2","text":"carries the ruleset into every model step while the mode is on.\n- Three zero-argument agent tools co"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"ntrol it:\n- `adhd_on` — enable for this session and persist (flag file under `$DSH_HOME/dsh-i-have-a"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"dhd/`)\n- `adhd_off` — disable and clear the flag\n- `adhd_status` — report state, since when, and whe"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"ther restart will restore it\n- The persisted flag restores the mode at boot.\n- The section registers"},{"id":"p10s6","text":" through the systemPrompt service, so toggling takes effect on the very next model step — no session"},{"id":"p10s7","text":" restart, no page refresh."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Install, then just say it in conversation:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"You can also ask for status any time, or create/remove the flag file yourself:\n`$DSH_HOME/dsh-i-have"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"-adhd/always-on` (default `~/.dsh/dsh-i-have-adhd/always-on`)."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## The ruleset"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Ten ideas, grouped for skimming — full text in `dsh/rules.js`:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"**Shape**: first line is the action · number the steps · close with one next move · park side quests"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"\n**State**: re-say where we are · estimate in real units · surface what now works\n**Tone**: errors a"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"re facts · cap lists at five · no throat-clearing"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Explicit overrides: harness rules outrank the mode; \"explain\" gets full depth with the same shape; d"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"estructive actions still confirm; a three-turn debug spiral triggers one diagnostic question instead"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ons still confirm; a three-turn debug spiral triggers one diagnostic question instead of more edits."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## How this differs from other ADHD plugins"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Two ADHD-related plugins already exist on the market, doing different jobs:\ndsh-adhd-copilot coaches"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" the user (task breakdown, launch rituals); adhdgofly-dsh-ext highlights parts of speech in rendered"},{"id":"p20s3","text":" Markdown. Neither touches how the assistant writes. This plugin shapes the assistant's own replies "},{"id":"p20s4","text":"— action-first structure, live on/off, restart persistence."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"MIT. Third-party notices: the concept and name derive from ayghri/i-have-adhd (MIT), whose license t"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ext is preserved in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
